I did not add the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`, and that clause is the node's entire authority. An approval mentioned in the request doesn't extend the grant. The grant has to change in the graph spec first, and then the world can import `http-client`. The fetch would also send raw input text into a URL query string unencoded, which is both an injection risk and a data leak to an external host. The files below implement the node as specified.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

